    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup for **Ghost Ride the WHIP** is anchored by a high-upside core, with **Corbin Carroll** leading the way at a robust 81.41 score. Facing Michael Lorenzen, **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a massive 14-point boost derived from his top-of-the-order slotting and favorable platoon alignment, making him the definitive play to hunt for those elusive stolen bases. Close behind, **Tyler Soderstrom** (73.03) and **Brice Turang** (72.43) offer immense value against weak starting pitching. **Brice Turang** in particular is a priority start today; his 19% bump from the favorable matchup against Sasaki, combined with an 8% boost for hitting second, makes him a primary catalyst for our Roto output. We also see strong reliability from **James Wood**, whose 70.10 score is buoyed by a prime leadoff spot and a high xwOBA, cementing his status as a foundational piece for this evening\u2019s slate.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Kyle Karros**, who flirted with our starting threshold at 51.91. While **Kyle Karros** projected well enough to be in the conversation, the optimizer ultimately pivoted to the superior situational utility of **Josh Naylor** and **Austin Riley**. **Austin Riley** is a particularly intriguing play today; despite a 67.43 score, he benefits from a rare \"Slow SP Delivery\" factor that historically increases stolen base opportunities for teammates, providing subtle hidden value. Conversely, we are keeping a close eye on **Henry Bolte** and **Tyler Soderstrom**, both of whom are confirmed as \"Lineup Pending.\" While we have built our projections around assumed spots for **Henry Bolte** (7th) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (5th), any late-shift downward in the order could drastically alter their daily efficiency. We are also monitoring **Vinnie Pasquantino** (60.32), who faces a stern test against Kirby; while he sits just above our starting floor, his high-leverage order spot keeps him in the lineup despite the tough SP_xERA. **Jose Caballero** remains sidelined due to the reported rainout, and we continue to navigate the absence of **Giancarlo Stanton** and others on the IL, alongside depth pieces like **Mickey Moniak**, **Trevor Story**, **Max Muncy**, **Dalton Rushing**, **Zach McKinstry**, **Alex Freeland**, and **Carson Williams**, who remain ready should our current starters falter.",
